# TypeScript

- Prefer explicit types on public APIs; infer locals where it stays clear.
- Handle errors deliberately — avoid empty `catch` blocks; log or rethrow with context.
- Keep components and modules focused; extract helpers when logic repeats.

```typescript
// Prefer narrow errors at boundaries
async function load(): Promise<Data> {
  const res = await fetch("/api/data");
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`load failed: ${res.status}`);
  return res.json() as Promise<Data>;
}
```
